# Ghost Robot still grid: 41/288; all 247 divergences are in the tile (corrected census, 2026-09-26)

commit:  main at 6f174d38 + the identity_diff.py fixes of this change
host:    i265 (Core Ultra 7 265K, 20 threads, 30 GiB, native Linux)
tool:    SVT_ORACLE=ghost-robot OSG_JOBS=4 tools/oracle_still_grid.sh
         (rows: gr_still_grid_2026-09-26.tsv, replaced by this run)

| first divergence | cells |
|------------------|-------|
| identical        | 41 (all 8-bit) |
| tile-op          | 166 |
| frame header     | 81, and ALL 81 also diverge in the tile (loop_filter_level, cdef strengths, lr_type: downstream of mode decision, per identity_diff's own guidance) |

CORRECTION. The first census below was produced by an identity_diff.py that
did not read qm_y/qm_u/qm_v after using_qmatrix = 1 (Ghost Robot's default),
so every frame-header field name after it was misread, and a coarse "tile"
stage then masked the op-level verdict. Both are fixed in the same change as
this record. The grst investigation (plan 3.3s, 0221442e) found the real
upstream: pre-deblock recon differs across the frame, so mode decision and
quantization diverge first.

---------------------------------------------------------------- superseded

# Ghost Robot still grid: 41/288, and where the other 247 first diverge (2026-09-26)

commit:  main at 2848742f (plan 3.3a landed); unchanged by b1fffbb3
host:    i265 (Core Ultra 7 265K, 20 threads, 30 GiB, native Linux)
tool:    SVT_ORACLE=ghost-robot OSG_JOBS=4 tools/oracle_still_grid.sh
         (tools/cellrun.py; rows: gr_still_grid_2026-09-26.tsv)
grid:    gradient + CID22 photo crop x {64,128,256} x bd {8,10} x qp {20,32,40,55}
         x presets {2,4,6,8,10,13}

| first divergence | cells |
|------------------|-------|
| identical        | 41 (all 8-bit; 0 of 144 10-bit cells) |
| tile-op          | 179 (99 CDF-symbol, 69 bool, 11 CDF-vs-bool) |
| tile payload     | 42 |
| frame header     | 26 (loop_filter_level, cdef_uv_pri_strength, lr_type, loop_filter_sharpness) |

Reading: function-level parity (c_parity 854/873) does not carry to stills.
The frame-header cells are the cheapest entry point (a DLF/CDEF/LR
derivation differs before any block is coded); the tile-op cells need the
first differing op localised per cell (`tools/identity_diff.py` reports it).
No 10-bit cell matches, so a bd10-specific Ghost Robot arm is likely.
